WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.248
- When would be able to tell your honey

00:00:02.248 --> 00:00:04.562
that I want to take you to the moon?

00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:05.727
- [Male Interviewer] 10 years.

00:00:05.727 --> 00:00:06.743
- 10 years.

00:00:06.743 --> 00:00:11.628
Entrepreneurs never feel their
ideas may or may not work

00:00:11.628 --> 00:00:13.106
and you know what entrepreneurs do?

00:00:13.106 --> 00:00:14.124
They pivot!

00:00:14.124 --> 00:00:15.286
In a business it's like a war.

00:00:15.286 --> 00:00:17.542
You have to be completely prepared.

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:19.601
It's not about the great vision

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.745
it's always about the great execution.

00:00:21.745 --> 00:00:24.587
- He's a business executive entrepreneur

00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:28.132
and founder and former CEO of InfoSpace.

00:00:28.132 --> 00:00:30.310
He's the cofounder of Moon Express,

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:33.580
a company that is making
machine-operated spacecraft

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.024
to try to go to the moon and harvest it

00:00:36.024 --> 00:00:37.490
for its raw materials.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:38.991
He's on track to potentially become

00:00:38.991 --> 00:00:41.057
the world's first trillionaire.

00:00:41.057 --> 00:00:43.054
He's Naveen Jain and here's my take

00:00:43.054 --> 00:00:44.974
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:44.974 --> 00:00:46.397
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:46.397 --> 00:00:48.333
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:49.746
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:49.746 --> 00:00:51.750
Also, as Naveen is talking
if he says something

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.969
that really, really resonates with you

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:54.646
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:54.646 --> 00:00:55.943
and put quotes around it

00:00:55.943 --> 00:00:59.860
so other people can be
inspired as well, enjoy.

00:01:01.896 --> 00:01:05.979
(inspirational orchestral music)

00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:14.243
(futuristic music)

00:01:15.871 --> 00:01:18.109
- [Narrator] At a compound
in Mountain View California

00:01:18.109 --> 00:01:21.563
internet billionaire Naveen
Jain is hatching a plan

00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:25.215
that could make him the
world's first trillionaire.

00:01:25.215 --> 00:01:27.935
- [Bob] Naveen, good to see you my friend.

00:01:27.935 --> 00:01:28.936
- [Naveen] Good.

00:01:28.936 --> 00:01:30.032
- So Naveen, the team is working hard

00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:31.339
as it usually is.

00:01:31.339 --> 00:01:32.351
- [Naveen] Of course.

00:01:32.351 --> 00:01:33.377
- [Bob] So we're going to land on the moon

00:01:33.377 --> 00:01:34.711
somewhere around here

00:01:34.711 --> 00:01:37.314
close to where the Apollo
spacecraft landed at the equator.

00:01:37.314 --> 00:01:38.590
- [Naveen] How did you pick that area?

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.793
- Well it's, first of
all it's on the near side

00:01:41.793 --> 00:01:43.088
so it's easily accessible from Earth.

00:01:43.088 --> 00:01:46.475
The dark area are actually
regions of lava plains

00:01:46.475 --> 00:01:48.721
so they're not mountainous.

00:01:48.721 --> 00:01:50.995
- [Narrator] Not so long
ago it was the Soviet

00:01:50.995 --> 00:01:53.028
and America superpowers
that were locked in a race

00:01:53.028 --> 00:01:54.427
to land on the moon.

00:01:54.427 --> 00:01:57.157
Now it's Bob and Naveen who
are leading the competition

00:01:57.157 --> 00:02:00.062
to mine precious metals from its surface.

00:02:00.062 --> 00:02:04.565
- Are we still on track to
land on the moon by 2015?

00:02:04.565 --> 00:02:05.610
- [Bob] We're still on track Naveen.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.468
- Initially we thought the
mission was going to cost us

00:02:08.468 --> 00:02:09.869
about $100,000,000.

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:11.680
Do you think we can bring the cost down

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.706
to say 50,000,000 to $60,000,000?

00:02:12.706 --> 00:02:14.189
- [Bob] Yeah, even less.

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:15.193
- Even less?

00:02:15.193 --> 00:02:16.193
- I think the first
mission will be under 50

00:02:16.193 --> 00:02:19.526
and subsequent missions may be under 40.

00:02:20.562 --> 00:02:23.244
- When would we be able to tell your honey

00:02:23.244 --> 00:02:25.436
that I want to take you to the moon?

00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:26.454
- [Bob] 10 years.

00:02:26.454 --> 00:02:27.483
- 10 years.

00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:28.493
- Not only will it be a honeymoon

00:02:28.493 --> 00:02:30.238
but I can take my honey to the moon,

00:02:30.238 --> 00:02:31.236
and I think that'll be the killer.

00:02:31.236 --> 00:02:32.248
- If you can do that,
that's real business.

00:02:32.248 --> 00:02:34.626
(laughs)

00:02:34.626 --> 00:02:37.959
If we can go to the moon for $50,000,000

00:02:38.881 --> 00:02:41.660
the cost comes down to 20
and we're able to bring back

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.410
the things worth $500,000,000,000

00:02:45.745 --> 00:02:50.652
I don't care what anybody
says, that's a great business.

00:02:50.652 --> 00:02:53.154
Somebody is going to create
a trillion dollar industry

00:02:53.154 --> 00:02:55.987
in space and we sure hope it's us.

00:02:57.131 --> 00:02:59.262
When you tell somebody what you're doing

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:01.362
and they don't think it's a crazy idea

00:03:01.362 --> 00:03:03.115
then you're thinking too small.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.214
So when you walk up to
a party and people say

00:03:05.214 --> 00:03:06.249
"What do you do?

00:03:06.249 --> 00:03:07.257
"Well, I mine the moon.

00:03:07.257 --> 00:03:08.865
"Well that's crazy.

00:03:08.865 --> 00:03:10.420
"Well, I'm thinking big."

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.854
As a young entrepreneur I
learned several valuable lessons

00:03:13.854 --> 00:03:15.880
but I think the most
valuable lesson I learned

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.876
was trusting your own gut instinct.

00:03:18.876 --> 00:03:22.900
It's not about the spreadsheets,
it's not about the numbers,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.716
it is about what you feel in your heart.

00:03:26.716 --> 00:03:31.128
Just remember there's so many
valuables in the real life,

00:03:31.128 --> 00:03:33.348
especially you can never capture them.

00:03:33.348 --> 00:03:36.762
The brain only works on
the logic of zeros and one

00:03:36.762 --> 00:03:38.327
and it doesn't know how

00:03:38.327 --> 00:03:39.989
to deal with a lot of the gray areas.

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:42.094
Your gut, your heart
is a chemical computer.

00:03:42.094 --> 00:03:46.261
It computes things on a fuzzy,
fuzzy magic, fuzzy logic.

00:03:47.963 --> 00:03:50.596
That means a lot of the
times you start to feel

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:52.056
that something doesn't feel right

00:03:52.056 --> 00:03:53.795
even though the numbers do add up.

00:03:53.795 --> 00:03:55.795
Never be afraid to fail.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.653
Entrepreneurs never fail.

00:04:00.617 --> 00:04:02.842
Their ideas may or may not work

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.720
and you know what entrepreneurs do?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.721
They pivot!

00:04:05.721 --> 00:04:09.819
Pivot is a way of saying I
have found a stepping stone

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:11.412
to even bigger success.

00:04:11.412 --> 00:04:16.245
So the way you do that is
always never let the ideas

00:04:16.245 --> 00:04:21.001
that has not worked become
the failure of a person.

00:04:21.001 --> 00:04:23.149
You are the person
becomes better every time

00:04:23.149 --> 00:04:26.300
and the more have you feel
the more arrows in your back

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.941
so after a third time you
can go to anyone and say,

00:04:28.941 --> 00:04:30.702
"Sir, I am the right CEO

00:04:30.702 --> 00:04:34.212
"because I know exactly what
not do to three times over."

00:04:34.212 --> 00:04:37.707
I wake up about 4:30 and five
and between five and 5:15.

00:04:37.707 --> 00:04:41.036
I am working on email,
catching up on news,

00:04:41.036 --> 00:04:43.446
looking at the blogs, looking
at the different opinions

00:04:43.446 --> 00:04:45.537
because people just don't sleep.

00:04:45.537 --> 00:04:46.722
I mean they're working 24/7.

00:04:46.722 --> 00:04:48.934
Somewhere around the world
people are awake and working

00:04:48.934 --> 00:04:50.772
so you're always
constantly being bombarded

00:04:50.772 --> 00:04:54.130
with request information
or just sometimes news.

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:58.297
And so in the morning I wake
up and I take care of my mind.

00:04:59.193 --> 00:05:02.193
(soft techno music)

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.440
And then after that

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:08.374
I workout and that's
taking care of my body.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:11.961
(music covers dialog)

00:05:11.961 --> 00:05:13.570
And then I do meditate before I go to work

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.898
so that takes care of my soul.

00:05:15.898 --> 00:05:16.905
In a business is like a war

00:05:16.905 --> 00:05:19.797
you have to be completely prepared

00:05:19.797 --> 00:05:22.198
and unless you have mind, body, and soul

00:05:22.198 --> 00:05:25.603
really all ready for it you
just can't fight that battle.

00:05:25.603 --> 00:05:27.361
Don't limit yourself.

00:05:27.361 --> 00:05:30.282
Go out and pursue your dreams

00:05:30.282 --> 00:05:32.984
even if you know nothing
about what you're going to do,

00:05:32.984 --> 00:05:34.114
go out and do that.

00:05:34.114 --> 00:05:37.067
Every time you have a
self doubt just remember

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:39.276
that every single successful company

00:05:39.276 --> 00:05:41.611
goes through a near-death experience

00:05:41.611 --> 00:05:43.449
before they go out and become successful.

00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:44.771
It is the mindset.

00:05:44.771 --> 00:05:46.152
And also people talk about

00:05:46.152 --> 00:05:48.148
people are optimistic or pessimistic

00:05:48.148 --> 00:05:49.859
so they look at whether
the glass is half empty

00:05:49.859 --> 00:05:50.979
or half full.

00:05:50.979 --> 00:05:52.954
To me that's really the
wrong question to ask.

00:05:52.954 --> 00:05:56.147
The only thing you as an
entrepreneur should think about is

00:05:56.147 --> 00:05:57.886
do I want to fill this glass?

00:05:57.886 --> 00:06:00.440
And the next question you ask
what do I want to fill it with?

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:02.983
It doesn't matter what it looks like.

00:06:02.983 --> 00:06:05.770
Your job is to imagine and dream

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:07.399
about what you want it to be.

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:10.139
The biggest problems are
really the social problems

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:12.566
and if you can solve them
it's a massive opportunity.

00:06:12.566 --> 00:06:15.654
Dream so big that people
think you're crazy

00:06:15.654 --> 00:06:18.112
and never be afraid to fail.

00:06:18.112 --> 00:06:20.248
If you want to make a billion dollars

00:06:20.248 --> 00:06:23.481
all you have to do is solve
a $10,000,000,000 problem.

00:06:23.481 --> 00:06:24.754
So go out and find a way

00:06:24.754 --> 00:06:27.397
to provide the fresh
water to the humanity.

00:06:27.397 --> 00:06:31.056
Go out and find a clean
solution for energy.

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:33.658
Go out and find a solution to agriculture.

00:06:33.658 --> 00:06:35.590
Find a solution to poverty.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:38.409
All of these $100,000,000,000 problem.

00:06:38.409 --> 00:06:40.854
So don't them as a problem think of them

00:06:40.854 --> 00:06:42.005
as a great entrepreneur opportunity

00:06:42.005 --> 00:06:44.144
and solving any of these problems

00:06:44.144 --> 00:06:45.823
will make you a billionaire.

00:06:45.823 --> 00:06:48.443
Another valuable lesson I
learned was being persistent

00:06:48.443 --> 00:06:49.905
while being flexible.

00:06:49.905 --> 00:06:53.558
A lot of entrepreneurs
spend way too much time

00:06:53.558 --> 00:06:57.624
writing a business plan rather
than really doing things.

00:06:57.624 --> 00:07:01.859
As you're continue doing
execute you'll find new things.

00:07:01.859 --> 00:07:04.016
You will learn new valuables.

00:07:04.016 --> 00:07:06.969
The trick is to have your business plan

00:07:06.969 --> 00:07:10.146
which only provides you the
guidelines but not the roadmap

00:07:10.146 --> 00:07:13.475
because as you're going out
and doing things in real world

00:07:13.475 --> 00:07:17.800
you will find things will
never ever turn out to be

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.350
the way you expected them
when you started a business.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:22.374
Don't try to stick to your business plan

00:07:22.374 --> 00:07:25.202
or spend too much time
writing a business plan

00:07:25.202 --> 00:07:28.373
but learn as you're
executing on a business plan

00:07:28.373 --> 00:07:30.532
and you will find
yourself to be successful.

00:07:30.532 --> 00:07:33.004
- [Narrator] For Naveen the
billionaire formula is simple.

00:07:33.004 --> 00:07:35.226
- What makes a successful person?

00:07:35.226 --> 00:07:38.474
They go out and solve big problems.

00:07:38.474 --> 00:07:40.600
So you know how to make a billion dollars?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.809
You solve a $10,000,000,000 problem.

00:07:42.809 --> 00:07:44.937
- [Narrator] Having
already made his billions

00:07:44.937 --> 00:07:47.764
he now unashamedly wants
to use his business brain

00:07:47.764 --> 00:07:50.251
to change our world.

00:07:50.251 --> 00:07:54.208
- Let's focus on education,
healthcare, energy,

00:07:54.208 --> 00:07:56.403
shortage of water, shortage of food

00:07:56.403 --> 00:07:59.227
and I'm going to tell you how
innovation and entrepreneurship

00:07:59.227 --> 00:08:01.092
can solve each of these problems.

00:08:01.092 --> 00:08:03.141
Let's look at education.

00:08:03.141 --> 00:08:06.709
Imagine if you are able
to use a $25 tablet

00:08:06.709 --> 00:08:10.328
and build some type of a
game that's more effective

00:08:10.328 --> 00:08:13.800
than a private tutor and is more addictive

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.126
than the most addictive video game.

00:08:16.126 --> 00:08:19.108
Think about it, one day a child
is going to come to the mother

00:08:19.108 --> 00:08:21.866
and say, "Mom, can I just
play one more hour of math?

00:08:21.866 --> 00:08:24.299
"Because I enjoy it so much."

00:08:24.299 --> 00:08:26.389
- [Narrator] Naveen has
a knack of putting people

00:08:26.389 --> 00:08:28.007
under his spell.

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:29.009
Making his mission

00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:31.778
to solve some of mankind's
biggest problems seem plausible

00:08:31.778 --> 00:08:33.777
in space and on Earth.

00:08:33.777 --> 00:08:36.006
- What if we can build an
artificial intelligence system

00:08:36.006 --> 00:08:38.419
that can be used by a village girl?

00:08:38.419 --> 00:08:41.497
She will be able to go door
and able to diagnose a disease.

00:08:41.497 --> 00:08:43.479
There are no healthcare,
there's no hospitals,

00:08:43.479 --> 00:08:44.717
there are no doctors.

00:08:44.717 --> 00:08:46.090
- [Narrator] These are big ideas

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.185
that could turn a big profit

00:08:48.185 --> 00:08:50.873
but some of them seem a bit farfetched.

00:08:50.873 --> 00:08:53.128
- What if you take a
3D printer on the moon?

00:08:53.128 --> 00:08:56.330
And somebody can go out and send the DNA

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:59.813
of a bacteria or a virus
and we print it right there

00:08:59.813 --> 00:09:01.113
and leave it on the moon

00:09:01.113 --> 00:09:02.684
and watch it grow.

00:09:02.684 --> 00:09:04.555
- [Interviewer] These ideas,
they're a bit out there

00:09:04.555 --> 00:09:05.574
aren't they, Naveen?

00:09:05.574 --> 00:09:06.980
Don't people think you're just a bit mad?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.899
- The point is, the
reason they think it's mad

00:09:09.899 --> 00:09:11.823
because it's already,

00:09:11.823 --> 00:09:13.585
they don't know it's already happening.

00:09:13.585 --> 00:09:15.853
The things that used to be science fiction

00:09:15.853 --> 00:09:18.328
are now becoming science reality.

00:09:18.328 --> 00:09:20.928
So I think a lot of the times,

00:09:20.928 --> 00:09:23.410
and this is just, it's
totally off the topic,

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.771
but people come to the
conferences with agenda.

00:09:26.771 --> 00:09:28.221
They have a hidden agenda.

00:09:28.221 --> 00:09:29.964
They want to get something done.

00:09:29.964 --> 00:09:31.973
They want to be politically correct.

00:09:31.973 --> 00:09:34.454
They cannot be themselves
and they are told

00:09:34.454 --> 00:09:36.203
never be vulnerable.

00:09:36.203 --> 00:09:39.374
Imagine what you do not
build the deep relationship

00:09:39.374 --> 00:09:41.581
with a person unless
you can be vulnerable,

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:45.239
unless you can share your
emotional connection with a person

00:09:45.239 --> 00:09:47.260
you can never build deep connection.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.935
People measure their success
when they leave the conference

00:09:49.935 --> 00:09:51.687
how many business card they give

00:09:51.687 --> 00:09:53.375
and how many business card they collected.

00:09:53.375 --> 00:09:54.722
Guess what?

00:09:54.722 --> 00:09:57.842
If you ever think you
have more than five people

00:09:57.842 --> 00:10:00.124
that you met in the
conference that you think

00:10:00.124 --> 00:10:01.508
you have a friendship with,

00:10:01.508 --> 00:10:02.975
you have a friendship with no one.

00:10:02.975 --> 00:10:05.284
You have to spend time.

00:10:05.284 --> 00:10:07.321
You have to connect with people.

00:10:07.321 --> 00:10:09.588
You have to give yourself to them

00:10:09.588 --> 00:10:12.614
and you have to let
your heart in their hand

00:10:12.614 --> 00:10:14.428
and say, "I trust you."

00:10:14.428 --> 00:10:16.645
And when you do that that is the time

00:10:16.645 --> 00:10:18.120
you build the deep relationship

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.454
when you leave this conference,

00:10:19.454 --> 00:10:21.646
they become your lifelong friends.

00:10:21.646 --> 00:10:25.804
So make one, two, three, or
four those lifelong friends

00:10:25.804 --> 00:10:28.703
when you go to a conference,
find a like-minded person

00:10:28.703 --> 00:10:31.162
who is going out, is going
to go make the change,

00:10:31.162 --> 00:10:33.337
who's going to go out
in a journey with you

00:10:33.337 --> 00:10:35.533
to go out and change the world.

00:10:35.533 --> 00:10:39.393
To me doing well by doing
good is my philosophy.

00:10:39.393 --> 00:10:41.641
That means you can create a great venture

00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:43.065
and if the venture can do good

00:10:43.065 --> 00:10:46.645
that becomes a philanthropic
adventure for my perspective.

00:10:46.645 --> 00:10:50.283
To me you can't create a $10,000,000,000

00:10:50.283 --> 00:10:51.881
by solving a $1,000,000,000 problem.

00:10:51.881 --> 00:10:53.829
To me you have to go out

00:10:53.829 --> 00:10:56.255
and solve a $100,000,000,000 problem

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:59.008
and it so happens those
$100,000,000,000 problems

00:10:59.008 --> 00:11:02.556
are massive social problems
which are education,

00:11:02.556 --> 00:11:05.620
the healthcare, the
clean water, the energy.

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:10.277
And if you can go provide access
to education in healthcare

00:11:10.277 --> 00:11:12.545
to billions of people around the world

00:11:12.545 --> 00:11:15.348
and if you happen to make
$100,000,000,000 profit,

00:11:15.348 --> 00:11:16.418
my hat's off to you.

00:11:16.418 --> 00:11:18.355
That's a great venture and
that's what you want people to do

00:11:18.355 --> 00:11:22.612
is not to separate doing
well from doing good

00:11:22.612 --> 00:11:25.077
because you can do both,
and that's how you create

00:11:25.077 --> 00:11:27.706
scalable, sustainable change.

00:11:27.706 --> 00:11:29.562
Well the last and the most valuable lesson

00:11:29.562 --> 00:11:31.215
as an entrepreneur I learned

00:11:31.215 --> 00:11:34.222
was about the value of execution.

00:11:34.222 --> 00:11:37.896
Way too many people, way too many people

00:11:37.896 --> 00:11:40.600
spend too much time
thinking about the vision.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.110
We are taught that you have
to build a better mousetrap.

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:46.717
Every venture capitalist will tell you

00:11:46.717 --> 00:11:48.591
that to be a successful entrepreneur

00:11:48.591 --> 00:11:50.710
you need to breakthrough innovation.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:55.261
Well you have to assume none
of us or at least most of us

00:11:55.261 --> 00:11:58.001
are not the smartest people in the world.

00:11:58.001 --> 00:12:01.673
There are lots and lots of
great, great inventors out there.

00:12:01.673 --> 00:12:04.588
How are we going to be the person

00:12:04.588 --> 00:12:06.644
who is going to always
build a better mousetrap?

00:12:06.644 --> 00:12:08.250
Well, to be successful

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.621
you don't have to build
a better mousetrap.

00:12:10.621 --> 00:12:13.938
You just have to build
a different mousetrap

00:12:13.938 --> 00:12:16.597
and as long as you're executing well

00:12:16.597 --> 00:12:19.826
the business always comes
down to block and tackle.

00:12:19.826 --> 00:12:21.717
It's not about the great vision

00:12:21.717 --> 00:12:24.087
it's always about the great execution.

00:12:24.087 --> 00:12:28.254
And you can always succeed by
out executing your competitors

00:12:29.495 --> 00:12:32.904
not necessarily having the
best product in the marketplace

00:12:32.904 --> 00:12:34.424
and I think Microsoft is a great example

00:12:34.424 --> 00:12:37.518
where they took a same product

00:12:37.518 --> 00:12:39.240
that other people may have had

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:41.075
but they executed substantially better

00:12:41.075 --> 00:12:45.663
and today they're the market
leader in the industry.

00:12:45.663 --> 00:12:47.413
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:47.413 --> 00:12:49.700
I made this video because Ali asked me to

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:53.616
and thank you so much 'cause
this was one of the most fun

00:12:53.616 --> 00:12:55.614
and inspiring Top 10s that I
think we've ever put together.

00:12:55.614 --> 00:12:57.532
At least I was extremely inspired by it

00:12:57.532 --> 00:12:59.481
and I love all my Top 10s

00:12:59.481 --> 00:13:01.221
but this one was especially inspiring.

00:13:01.221 --> 00:13:02.856
So thank you so much for that ask.

00:13:02.856 --> 00:13:04.594
And if you guys have somebody

00:13:04.594 --> 00:13:06.026
that you'd like to see profiled next,

00:13:06.026 --> 00:13:08.279
a famous entrepreneur that
you want to be inspired by

00:13:08.279 --> 00:13:10.184
please leave it in the comments below

00:13:10.184 --> 00:13:11.578
and I'll see what I can do.

00:13:11.578 --> 00:13:13.314
I'd also love to know what rule

00:13:13.314 --> 00:13:15.170
had the biggest impact on you and why?

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.912
What lesson are you going
to apply to your life

00:13:16.912 --> 00:13:17.910
for business immediately?

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.225
Leave it in the comments below.

00:13:20.225 --> 00:13:21.635
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:13:21.635 --> 00:13:23.624
Finally I wanted to give a
quick shoutout to Mihovil.

00:13:23.624 --> 00:13:25.410
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.774
"Your One Word" it really, really, really

00:13:27.774 --> 00:13:28.779
means a lot to me.

00:13:28.779 --> 00:13:29.875
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:13:29.875 --> 00:13:31.169
I believe in you.

00:13:31.169 --> 00:13:32.910
I hope you continue to
believe in yourselves

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:37.077
and whatever your one is,
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:13:44.465 --> 00:13:46.332
- Think differently.

00:13:46.332 --> 00:13:48.614
It's not about thinking outside the box

00:13:48.614 --> 00:13:51.316
it's about thinking in a different box.

00:13:51.316 --> 00:13:54.110
If you become an expert in your field

00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:57.209
you become absolutely
useless in your field

00:13:57.209 --> 00:13:59.201
because the day you become an expert

00:13:59.201 --> 00:14:01.013
you become incrementalist.

00:14:01.013 --> 00:14:02.923
You think about incremental evolution.

00:14:02.923 --> 00:14:04.791
So if you want to disrupt something

00:14:04.791 --> 00:14:07.075
go out in a completely different industry

00:14:07.075 --> 00:14:08.309
that you know nothing about

00:14:08.309 --> 00:14:10.291
because then you're thinking abstract.

00:14:10.291 --> 00:14:14.060
So never be afraid to
talk about your problem

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:16.544
to someone who knows
nothing about your industry

00:14:16.544 --> 00:14:18.367
because they will come up with the ways

00:14:18.367 --> 00:14:19.711
that you have never thought before.

00:14:19.711 --> 00:14:22.711
Making money is a
byproduct of doing things

00:14:22.711 --> 00:14:24.294
that you really enjoy doing,

00:14:24.294 --> 00:14:26.906
it is never a goal in itself.

00:14:26.906 --> 00:14:29.653
And it's like having sex and orgasm,

00:14:29.653 --> 00:14:33.434
you have to enjoy the process
and not focus on the end goal.

00:14:33.434 --> 00:14:35.619
People actually who focus on end goal

00:14:35.619 --> 00:14:37.458
like getting an orgasm never get one.

00:14:37.458 --> 00:14:41.134
As I was in college I learned
a couple of valuable lessons

00:14:41.134 --> 00:14:43.909
one of them was passion.

00:14:43.909 --> 00:14:45.585
We have a lot of distractions in life

00:14:45.585 --> 00:14:47.963
but there's some things that
are really important to us.

00:14:47.963 --> 00:14:51.104
We spend our waking hours
and our sleeping time

00:14:51.104 --> 00:14:53.765
all thinking about that particular thing.

00:14:53.765 --> 00:14:56.216
Once you find that passion you will find

00:14:56.216 --> 00:15:00.788
that it's no longer a
work it becomes your life,

00:15:00.788 --> 00:15:01.968
it consumes you.

00:15:01.968 --> 00:15:04.286
So find something that you're
really, really excited about

00:15:04.286 --> 00:15:06.155
and devote your life to it.

